-- ============================================================================
-- PD3 PROFESSIONAL DEEP SEED: ESP Design, intermediate tier.
--
-- Six modules, 26 lessons, 132 questions (15 per module bank plus a 42
-- question final exam). The structure row is GENERATED from the tier's
-- manifest.json rather than hand typed.
--
-- What this tier owns: THE FLUID AND THE LIFT. What the pump actually sees at
-- its intake, and how a well becomes a head requirement and a stage count.
--
-- STAGES ARE INTEGERS, AND THAT IS THE RESULT THE EXPERT TIER IS BUILT ON.
-- `stageCount` rounds UP, so the stack always makes more head than it was
-- asked for, and the two brake powers that follow differ by EXACTLY
-- `headMadeFt / tdhFt`. That is an identity, not an approximation: it holds to
-- 1e-16 on every case in the course and across a fifteen step requirement
-- sweep. The margin is therefore bounded by ONE STAGE and not by a percentage,
-- so it GROWS AS THE STACK SHRINKS: 0.037359 percent on 192 stages, 0.109901
-- on 264, 0.580425 on 172, 2.567658 on 33. A reviewer who calls it rounding
-- noise has missed that the short shallow pump, the one most likely to be
-- waved through, is where it is largest.
--
-- THE DECOMPOSITION CLOSES, AND THE CLOSURE IS NOT A CHECK. Total dynamic head
-- is the net lift plus the tubing friction plus the wellhead term, and on every
-- case the three sum to the head the two pressures gave, to 1e-12. But
-- `tdhBreakdown` SUMS THE THREE TERMS IT IS HANDED and never returns to the
-- pressures, so that closure is a property of how the parts were derived and
-- not a test the package performs. A number that adds up perfectly can still
-- be wrong in all three of its parts.
--
-- ONE CONVENTION, ADJUDICATED AND DELIBERATELY LEFT ALONE. The module holds
-- two forms of one conversion: `gradientFromDensity` divides by 144 while
-- `PSI_PER_FT_SG` is the rounded 0.433, and 62.4/144 is 0.433333, so the two
-- are 0.076982 percent apart. Engines PR #109 examined five findings in this
-- domain and changed exactly one, and this was not it, because both the
-- goldens and the live application derive the specific gravity from the DESIGN
-- GRADIENT, so the two routes never meet on a shipped case. The tier teaches
-- the convention as a convention and says plainly that knowing which defects
-- you are allowed to fix is part of the job.
--
-- AND TWO GAS THRESHOLDS, ONLY ONE OF WHICH IS EVER COMPARED AGAINST. The
-- stream gas volume fraction and the fraction through the pump are different
-- numbers, and the handler and separator limits are applied to the second. A
-- reader quoting "the GVF" without saying which one has said nothing.
--
-- The numbers that travel to the next tier are the head requirement, the stage
-- count, and the two brake powers that the integer rounding pulled apart.
-- ============================================================================

